/**
 * @page gettingstarted Getting Started
 *
 * @brief Basics of the engine and syntax with examples.
 *
 * @section creatingwindow Creating a window
 *
 * To create a window with s.eng lib, you'll need to instantiate an object of the class seng::window.
 * Basically, this class contains all of the code to create a window and managing it.
 *
 * Its constructor has some parameters. You need to define width, height and the name of the window (title)
 * 
 * See this basic window object:
 * @code
 * seng::window my_window(640, 360, "framebyframehihi");
 * @endcode
 *
 * This line of code creates the window object with width of 640, height of 360 and its title as 'framebyframehihi'.
 *
 * The next step is the Game Loop. Your window needs to stay open and listen to when it needs to close (you clicked the close button in your OS).
 * The seng::window class provides a glfw wrapper function for this, seng::window::shouldClose()
 *
 * Other important thing is to update the events. Every "action" is an event and it needs to be updated everytime.
 *
 * @code
 * while (!window.shouldClose()) {
    window.eventUpdate();

    seng::renderer::clear(seng::vec4<double>(1.0, 1.0, 0.0, 1.0));

    window.drawUpdate();
  }
 * @endcode
 *
 * seng::window::eventUpdate() updates the events. Note that we put other function: seng::renderer::clear. Basically, this function "paints" (or clears)
 * the entire window with the color in the first parameter.
 *
 * Entire example:
 * @ref example_window.cpp
 * 
  */
